From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Axel Garcia K." <git@axelgk.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 10:33:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] state: rebuild events after restoring counters

Load the complete counter snapshot before rebasing the event queue so the next VBlank remains reachable after cross-process restoration.

Evidence: this is the previously reviewed frontend patch qpsx-savestate-resume.patch, applied in its established build order on upstream 368310a.

Risk: limited to the paths recorded in that patch. Reverting this commit restores the preceding independently buildable checkpoint.
---
 src/misc.cpp | 12 ++++++------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/misc.cpp b/src/misc.cpp
index ce469289e0aa074a804c4fb8bb2683b9c87dda52..0efba0fc3e0ffcc0dda15ee8799adc9a55e6b482 100644
--- a/src/misc.cpp
+++ b/src/misc.cpp
@@ -922,12 +922,6 @@ int LoadState(const char *file) {
 	psxRegs.psxH=psxH;
 	psxRegs.io_cycle_counter=0;
 
-	//senquack - Clear & intialize new event scheduler queue based on
-	// saved contents of psxRegs.interrupt and psxRegs.intCycle[]
-	// NOTE: important to do this before calling any functions like
-	// psxRcntFreeze() that will queue events of their own.
-	psxEvqueueInitFromFreeze();
-
 	if (Config.HLE)
 		psxBiosFreeze(0);
 
@@ -968,6 +962,12 @@ int LoadState(const char *file) {
 	     mdecFreeze(f, FREEZE_LOAD)     )
 		goto error;
 
+	/* Rebuild only after rcnts[] has been restored.  This routine rebases
+	 * psxRegs.cycle to zero and adjusts root-counter timestamps; doing it
+	 * before psxRcntFreeze() adjusts stale counters and then overwrites them
+	 * with unrebased values from the state. */
+	psxEvqueueInitFromFreeze();
+
 	//XXX: HACK December 2016 -- see comment above
 skip_missing_data_hack:
 
